			"notes": "- Completely refactored the underlying rendering logic, shifting from CPU Rasterization with Texture Caching to Direct GPU Hardware-Accelerated Rendering, transferring a portion of rendering entirely to the GPU and resulting in a massive performance boost of 3x-4x\n- Added an experimental auto-update feature, allowing players to also manually check for updates using /PVPUtils update (requires a stable network connection)\n- Added Armor Status display\n- Added Potion Effects display\n- Added motion blur with an optimized algorithm\n- Added New style to keystrokes\n- Added elytra improvements and critical hit assist\n- Added five background GLSLs\n- Added FOV fog removal and vignette removal\n- Added a player-only option for the nametag feature\n- Added built-in fix for the MC-159163 bug\n- Fixed an issue causing abnormal block-hitting animations\n- Fixed an issue where certain UI elements would flicker, display with incorrect shapes and sizes, or have inverted text under specific scenarios\n- Fixed a rendering issue where ClickGUI would not display properly when shown simultaneously with Notifications\n- Fixed an issue in HUDEdit where the rule of thirds grid and element borders would sometimes not display or become misaligned\n- Fixed an issue where the language would not automatically change based on the user's current system language\n- Fixed occasional crashes related to the GLSL renderer and several other crash issues\n- Fixed various compatibility bugs from previous alpha and beta versions\n- Optimized file structure to reduce package size by approximately half\n- Reduced runtime memory (RAM) usage\n- Improved and updated the Terms of Service (ToS)\n- Removed certain legacy features"
